course: dictionary
lesson: 5170
title: Islanders and where people live
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An islander is a person who lives on an island, or was born on one. It is a noun, so it names a person. Ask yourself: is this person on an island, or from one?
explain: Read this: «Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples have lived in Australia for at least 50,000 to 65,000 years, among the oldest continuing cultures in the world.» Torres Strait Islander is a name for peoples connected to the Torres Strait islands. The word islander is part of that name, and the clue is the island.
explain: The sentences do not say that every person in a place is an islander. The word only fits people who live on an island or were born on one. Check by swapping in the meaning: "a person who lives on an island" should still make sense in the sentence.
fact: An islander is a person who lives on an island, or was born on one.
fact: Islander is a noun: one islander, many islanders.
fact: «Torres Strait Islander» is a name for peoples connected to the Torres Strait islands, in Australia.
fact: Other examples are Pacific Islanders, the people of the Scottish islands, and Channel Islanders.
fact: Stories about islanders often mention ferries, fishing and the sea.
exercise: What does islander mean? | *A person who lives on an island, or was born on one | A ferry boat captain | A fish that swims near the coast | A high mountain climber
exercise: Find the word in «Torres Strait Islander peoples» that means a person from an island. | *Islander | Strait | Torres | peoples
exercise: Which sentence shows an islander? | Ella lives in a big city far from the sea | *Ella lives on a small Scottish island and takes the ferry to school | Ella lives in a tent in the forest | Ella climbs the mountain behind her house
test: Tom was born on the Isle of Skye and still lives there. What is he? | *An islander | A sailor | A shepherd who only works in the city | A farmer
test: Which word is the noun in «The islanders waved from the ferry»? | *islanders | waved | from | ferry
exam: What does islander mean? | A boat that carries people across the sea | *A person who lives on an island or was born on one | An island with lots of hills | A word that means very wet
